    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Parallel Vectors",
    "problem": "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=⟨-1,-2⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨3,6⟩.$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6-3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6+6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$",
